  "cards": [
    { "dot": "cyan", "title": "The warm path is one round trip", "items": [
      "An unchanged environment answers 304 with no body, before the snapshot is ever loaded.",
      "A warm read costs one indexed Environment row plus one Redis GET, and no flag query at all.",
      "Concurrent checks collapse into one request: a read lock plus a refresh counter makes the read single-flight."
    ] },
    { "dot": "rose", "title": "Why a miss can never be stale", "items": [
      "The cached entry stores the environment version, so a mismatch is a miss rather than a stale read.",
      "SNAPSHOT_CACHE_TTL is only a backstop for a mutation that forgot to bump the version.",
      "Every Redis helper swallows errors and reports a miss, so a cache outage is a slowdown, never a 500."
    ] }
  ]
